<title>POLAND: Polish insurer Hestia increases share capital.</title>
<headline>Polish insurer Hestia increases share capital.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Polish insurer STU Hestia Insurance SA, 88-percent owned by Alte Leipziger Europa, have decided to raise their firm's share capital to 43.7 million zlotys from 34.7 million, Hestia said.</p>
<p>The firm said in a statement on Friday that its current owners would take all the new shares.</p>
<p>Bank Gdanski has 5.5 percent of Hestia shares and the rest are held by several Polish institutions and individuals.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
